issue_context.body:
Using Sway 1.5, on Gentoo and Arch linux

```
output DP-1 {
  subpixel rgb
}
font pango:monospace 10
bar {
  status-command ~/mystatus.sh
}
```

At this point, subpixel blending will be used by sway for window titles/decoration, but not by swaybar to draw text. Swaybar keeps using grayscale AA, even though subpixel seems to be what's wanted by render code in both cases

Testing shows that Cairo will bail out of subpixel AA if the cairo_operator is set to SOURCE. Changing swaybar to use the default OVER "fixes" it, and results in use of subpixel blending for text

Is it Cairo that could be wrong ? Changing to OVER "feels right" because AA will require blending anyway, yet the manual lets one feel that active operator and anti-aliasing modes shouldn't interfere with each other (internal requirements of AA not caller's problem)
